# Force LF line endings on checkout for all text files.
# The OpenWrt Makefile uses backslash line-continuations in Build/Compile; a
# trailing CR before '\' makes GNU make miss the continuation and breaks the
# Rust cross-build.  Shell scripts and the bundled Rust sources must also stay
# LF.  Without this, git's core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) re-adds CRLF
# on every checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark the build/shell critical files as text even if content
# sniffing ever disagrees.
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
